      "5191b703f925f3ef": {
        "_id": "5191b703f925f3ef",
        "folder": null,
        "img": "systems/pf1/icons/items/weapons/dagger.PNG",
        "name": "Dagger, Alchemical Silver",
        "system": {
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>A dagger is a fighting knife. Its blade is usually less than 1 foot long, and can be curved or straight, with one edge or two. Dagger designs vary widely, and can have many different names (such as a thrusting dagger being called a \"dirk\"). You get a +2 bonus on Sleight of Hand skill checks made to conceal a dagger on your body.</p><p>This dagger is treated with alchemical silver. Silvered piercing and slashing weapons deal 1 less damage on a successful attack (minimum 1). This material modifier awaits the later automation review.</p><hr><p>Compendium adaptation: Pathfinder 1 11.11. <a href=\"https://gitlab.com/foundryvtt_pathfinder1e/foundryvtt-pathfinder1\">Source project</a>. Rules: Open Game Content (OGL 1.0a).</p>",
            "instructions": "",
            "unidentified": "<p>A dagger is a fighting knife. Its blade is usually less than 1 foot long, and can be curved or straight, with one edge or two. Dagger designs vary widely, and can have many different names (such as a thrusting dagger being called a \"dirk\"). You get a +2 bonus on Sleight of Hand skill checks made to conceal a dagger on your body.</p>"
